        "original_id": "bcd0bd15-fe6a-5501-ace4-25e788c5c7ef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-François Clervoy, Thomas Reiter\n- Organizations: CNES, ESA, NASA, German Air Force\n- Missions: NASA Space Shuttle missions, STS-121, Expedition 14\n- Places: Frankfurt, West Germany, International Space Station\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-François André Clervoy was born on 19 November 1958 and is a French engineer, a CNES astronaut, and an ESA astronaut.\n- Thomas Arthur Reiter was born on 23 May 1958 in Frankfurt, West Germany.\n- Jean-François Clervoy is a veteran of three NASA Space Shuttle missions.\n- Thomas Reiter is a retired European astronaut and a Brigadier General in the German Air Force.\n- Thomas Reiter arrived at the International Space Station on 6 July 2006 aboard Space Shuttle Discovery during mission STS-121.\n- Thomas Reiter was serving as ESA Interagency Coordinator and Advisor to the Director General at the European Space Agency.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
